 "literal": "Even to the town, near indeed is the pond. / Even far, it is not indeed, the small forest river. / Except for the white heron seeking prey, at all / approaching is gone in the grove. We, our / short hair for, cleansing clay to bring, will go. / There also, she will come, the very innocent girl.",
 "translation": "The pond is very close to the town, and the small forest river is not far from the pond. No one ever enters the grove there, except the white heron looking for prey. We are going there to fetch cleansing clay for our short hair. She too, that very innocent girl, will come there.",
 "modern": "ஊருக்கு மிக அருகில் பொய்கை இருக்கிறது. அந்தப் பொய்கைக்கு மிக அருகில் காட்டாறு இருக்கிறது. இரை தேடும் வெள்ளைக் குருகைத் தவிர வேறு யாரும் அந்தச் சோலைக்குள் செல்வதில்லை. நாங்கள் எங்களுடைய குட்டையான கூந்தலைத் தூய்மை செய்ய நெய்மண் கொண்டுவர அங்குச் செல்கிறோம். மிகவும் பேதையான அவளும் அங்கு வருவாள்.",
 "explanation": "The friend is speaking to the hero within his hearing to suggest a secret meeting place with the heroine. She describes a secluded grove near a forest river, which is close to the town's pond. This grove is extremely private, visited only by a white heron searching for prey, meaning they will not be disturbed by others. By mentioning that they are going there to gather cleansing clay for their hair and that the innocent heroine will accompany them, the friend subtly invites the hero to meet her there. The imagery of the quiet grove and the solitary heron belongs to the Marutam landscape, highlighting the theme of secret trysts and the intimacy of the lovers.",
